WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.810
April 25, 2015.

2
00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:07.030
A magnitude 7.8 earthquake
strikes Gorkha, Nepal.

3
00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:12.470
The quake and its aftershocks set
off at least 25,000 landslides.

4
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.970
Roads and villages may be cut off.

5
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:17.190
Relief teams need to know where.

6
00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:20.110
How could people help map
where help was needed?

7
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:22.730
Or could nobody help from far away?

8
00:00:22.780 --> 00:00:26.590
In this mission, you'll sort the
ways geographers collect data:

9
00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:31.410
in the field, with technology, and
from written sources like interviews.

10
00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.990
Then you'll see how decisions
based on data change places,

11
00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:38.470
and what happens to people the data miss.

12
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:43.810
Your mission: find out how people helped map
where help was needed after the earthquake.
